{"id":"scripts/ocr-consensus.ts","pkg":"scripts","kind":"script","lines":220,"commentLines":23,"header":["Consensus correction of the stored circular text. For every page, the stored text (read by the pipeline's OCR) is compared word by word with the readings of two other independent readers of the SAME page image (Gemini 3.1 Pro and Gemini 3.8 Flash, already saved in reread-cache/gemini by scripts/gemini-read-archive.ts). My rule: a number, date, amount, phone or clause number of the stored text is replaced ONLY when BOTH readers propose the same replacement for the same place; a word is never changed (it is reported). See src/lib/ingestion/consensusPatch.ts for every rule. DRY RUN (default): writes nothing to the database and calls no Gemini; saves reread-reports/consensus-<time>.json and .md npx tsx --env-file=.env.local scripts/ocr-consensus.ts [--ids 34,20,31] APPLY: for every circular that passes the gate, backs it up (reread-backups/), replaces its chunks (new vectors), reads them back, and re-checks them. npx tsx --env-file=.env.local scripts/ocr-consensus.ts --apply [--ids ...] The gate (a circular is applied only if all hold): no patch crosses a chunk boundary; every replacement number is present in BOTH readers' text; after the patches the circular has no MORE unconfirmed numbers than before; no roster page (stored as rows) is touched."],"symbols":[{"name":"PRO","kind":"constant","exported":false,"line":27,"sig":"const PRO = \"gemini:gemini-3.1-pro-preview\"","type":"","doc":["These are names of saved readings only: this script makes no model call; it reads the cache files that earlier readings left under these names (src/lib/ai/noPro.selftest.ts lists it as the one file that may name a Pro model)."],"members":[],"items":0,"id":"f85081c6f8-PRO","usedBy":[]},{"name":"FLASH","kind":"constant","exported":false,"line":28,"sig":"const FLASH = \"gemini:gemini-3.8-flash\"","type":"","doc":[],"members":[],"items":0,"id":"f85081c6f8-FLASH","usedBy":[]},{"name":"ar